  The reel_script and caption say the 205 homes were built in 2020 as the apartment complex, but the article says the apartments were built in 2020 and the 205 homes were part of that project; this is a minor framing, but the caption also says the 10% open space was from the housing project of 205 homes, which is acceptable. However, the caption claims the 205-home complex's land had 10% open space, which the article states as the project land — no clear error there.
  The reel_script states the land was given via thanap pathiram (gift deed) 'to the Chennai Corporation' in July 2020, which matches the article; no problem there.
  The reel_script says 'மேலும் செய்திகளுக்கு' is fine; no issue.
  The reel_script omits the claim that private persons say the land belongs to them and that the housing board wrongly handed it over, an important point of the article about who is occupying and their stated reason (missing fact).
  The caption's 'அங்கு வீட்டுவசதி வாரியம் 2020ல் கட்டிய 205 வீடுகள் உள்ள அடுக்குமாடி குடியிருப்புகளின் திட்ட நிலத்தில் 10 சதவீதம்' sentence is garbled: it mixes the project's homes and the land share in a confusing way, and does not clearly convey that the 10% open-space reservation was for the project land.
